      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T08:42:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I adopted Kyle\u0027s lazy atomic allocation approach. However, it wasn\u0027t clear to me whether we want the lazy allocation happens in the `ObjectLabel` class itself or in `ApiObjectBase`.\n\nFrom http://crbug.com/479457809#comment2, it looks like Corentin prefers to have separate `ObjectLabel` allocation to support future deduplications, so I chose the latter. Otherwise, we would have had 2 heap allocations (1 for ObjectLabel and 1 for its inner Impl).\n\n\u003e we could make it return a mutex guard for the label\n\nanw, I also thought about this but returning a scoped mutex + string could increase the locked scope and potentially add lock inversion risks that are hard to control.",
      "parentUuid": "066f8d6a_e67e84e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 205,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "65567a51fc510fa9513a4a3fda8d1cf6bdd516df",
