      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T13:23:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Otherwise, we would have had 2 heap allocations (1 for ObjectLabel and 1 for its inner Impl).\n\nHere is what I was thinking originally. The current `ObjectLabel` class just has to become `ObjectLabel::Impl` and the logic that was added in `ApiObjectBase` moves into a new `ObjectLabel` class. `ApiObjectBase` owns a `ObjectLabel` directly with no heap allocations. `ObjectLabel` owns the `std::atomic\u003cImpl*\u003e` which has one heap allocation. I think that is the same number of heap allocations and the logic is encapsulated in it\u0027s own class that can be tested independently.\n\nFWIW it\u0027s easy to make that change as a follow up and this is going to be a big improvement already.",
      "parentUuid": "aedb5867_ff755d8a",
      "range": {
